---
/**
 * /terms — Terms of Use.
 *
 * Built Aug 26 2026 from docs/legal/terms.md, which Fredrick supplied the same day. It
 * replaces the unreviewed Aug 24 draft of the same name.
 *
 * HELD ON A BRANCH with /privacy and /data-handling. NOT FOR MERGE UNTIL COUNSEL HAS READ
 * IT. The copy file heads itself "Draft for legal review. Do not publish as written".
 * `noindex` is set and the page is filtered out of the sitemap, but neither is the hold —
 * a page reachable from the footer is public whether or not a crawler indexes it.
 *
 * WHAT THIS PAGE IS, AND IS NOT. These are terms for using the website. They are NOT the
 * client contract. The engagement agreement governs paid work and takes precedence
 * wherever the two touch — section 10 says so explicitly, and THAT SECTION IS WHY THIS
 * PAGE IS SAFE TO PUBLISH BEFORE THE ENGAGEMENT AGREEMENT IS FINISHED. If section 10 is
 * ever trimmed as boilerplate, that stops being true.
 *
 * SECTION 3 IS THE COMMERCIALLY IMPORTANT ONE and it must not be trimmed either. The site
 * publishes two figures — from CAD $1,000 on /workshop and from CAD $4,000 on /workshop
 * and /accounting. Section 3 is what keeps a published figure from being treated as an
 * offer capable of acceptance. Most small-firm website terms do not need it; this one
 * does.
 *
 * SECTION 3 AND THE PRICING COPY HAVE TO STAY IN STEP. If a page ever drops the word
 * "from", publishes a payment schedule, or names a figure for a specific deliverable, this
 * section stops covering it. "From" is load-bearing on the pricing pages for a commercial
 * reason and load-bearing here for a legal one.
 *
 * TWO DEPARTURES FROM THE APPROVED COPY, both matching the calls taken on /privacy and
 * /data-handling on Aug 26 2026:
 *
 * 1. NO LOCATION LINE. The draft prints "based in Metro Vancouver, British Columbia,
 *    Canada" in the opening and again in the section 14 contact block. Both are gone under
 *    the standing instruction of Aug 25 2026.
 *
 *    SECTION 12 IS NOT AN EXCEPTION TO THAT AND MUST NOT BE STRIPPED WITH IT. "Governed by
 *    the laws of the Province of British Columbia" is a choice-of-law clause, not a
 *    sentence about where the business sits. Removing it would not tidy a location line;
 *    it would delete the governing law and leave the document without one, which is a
 *    different and much worse thing. The no-location rule is about how the site describes
 *    itself to a reader. This names the law that applies.
 *
 * 2. NO mailto:. Section 14 shows the address as text, per the standing rule that no
 *    mailto: remains anywhere on the site.
 *
 * ONE BLANK, and it is not guessed: the jurisdiction of incorporation, shared with
 * /privacy through PENDING in src/lib/legal.ts. Everything else this page's [CONFIRM] list
 * raises is a question for counsel rather than a hole in the copy — whether a liability
 * cap belongs in section 9 or only in the engagement agreement, whether disputes should
 * match the engagement agreement's mechanism rather than section 12's BC courts, and
 * whether BC's Business Practices and Consumer Protection Act is confirmed not to apply to
 * business-to-business work. NONE of those changes what is on the page today; all three
 * change what counsel may ask for.
 *
 * THE REGISTER IS DELIBERATE. Sections 1 to 4 are written in plain English because the
 * same reader who reads /accounting reads this, and a page that suddenly sounds like a
 * different company undoes the work every other page does. Where counsel genuinely
 * requires particular wording, take counsel's wording. Where they do not, keep the plain
 * version.
 */
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import LegalDocument from "../components/legal/LegalDocument.astro";
import Pending from "../components/legal/Pending.astro";
import {
  PENDING,
  LEGAL_EFFECTIVE_DATE,
  LEGAL_ENTITY,
  LEGAL_EMAIL,
} from "../lib/legal";

const description =
  "The terms that govern use of arksystems.ca — what the site is, what published prices mean, and how these terms sit alongside an engagement agreement.";
---

<BaseLayout title="Terms of Use" description={description} noindex>
  <LegalDocument
    title="Terms of Use"
    dateline={`Effective ${LEGAL_EFFECTIVE_DATE}. Last updated ${LEGAL_EFFECTIVE_DATE}.`}
  >
    <p>
      These terms govern your use of arksystems.ca. By using this website you accept them. If
      you do not accept them, please do not use the site.
    </p>

    <p>
      ArkSystems is operated by {LEGAL_ENTITY}, a company incorporated in{" "}
      <Pending value={PENDING.incorporatedIn} label="jurisdiction of incorporation" />. In
      these terms, &ldquo;ArkSystems&rdquo;, &ldquo;we&rdquo; and &ldquo;us&rdquo; mean{" "}
      {LEGAL_ENTITY} operating as ArkSystems. &ldquo;You&rdquo; means the person or business
      using the site.
    </p>

    <h2 id="what-this-website-is">1. What this website is</h2>

    <p>
      This website describes what ArkSystems does and how we work. It is provided for
      information.
    </p>

    <p>
      Nothing on this site is professional advice. We are not accountants, lawyers, tax
      advisers or auditors, we hold no professional designation, and nothing here should be
      relied on as advice about your own business, your finances, your tax position or your
      legal obligations. Decisions about your business remain yours, and where they require
      professional advice you should obtain it from a qualified professional.
    </p>

    <h2 id="no-guarantee">2. No guarantee of outcome</h2>

    <p>
      We describe what AI systems do and what an engagement involves. We do not promise a
      particular result, a saving, a return, or a level of performance in your business, and
      nothing on this site should be read as such a promise.
    </p>

    <p>
      Where an engagement is agreed, what we commit to is set out in the engagement agreement
      for that work, and only there.
    </p>

    <h2 id="prices">3. Prices shown on this site</h2>

    <p>
      Any figure published on this site is a starting point, not a quotation and not an offer
      capable of acceptance.
    </p>

    <p>
      &ldquo;From CAD $1,000&rdquo; and &ldquo;from CAD $4,000&rdquo; mean the minimum at
      which that kind of work begins. What a specific piece of work costs depends on its
      scope, and is quoted to you in writing after we understand what is involved. A price
      becomes binding only when it appears in a written agreement signed by both of us.
    </p>

    <p>All figures are in Canadian dollars and exclude applicable taxes.</p>

    <h2 id="booking">4. Booking a call</h2>

    <p>
      Booking a call through this site reserves time in a calendar. It creates no contract, no
      obligation on either of us, and no commitment to buy or to sell anything. Either of us
      may cancel or reschedule.
    </p>

    <h2 id="our-content">5. Our content</h2>

    <p>
      Everything on this site &mdash; text, images, illustrations, layout, the ArkSystems
      name, logo and tagline &mdash; belongs to ArkSystems or is used with permission, and is
      protected by copyright and trade-mark law.
    </p>

    <p>
      You may read it, print it, and share links to it. You may not republish it, sell it, or
      use it as your own material, and you may not use the ArkSystems name, logo or tagline
      without our written permission.
    </p>

    <p>
      Ownership of anything produced during a paid engagement &mdash; a workshop document, a
      specification, a built system &mdash; is dealt with in the engagement agreement, not
      here.
    </p>

    <h2 id="acceptable-use">6. Acceptable use</h2>

    <p>Please do not:</p>

    <ul>
      <li>Use the site for anything unlawful</li>
      <li>Attempt to gain unauthorized access to the site or anything connected to it</li>
      <li>Interfere with the site&rsquo;s operation or its availability to others</li>
      <li>
        Collect information from the site by automated means for commercial purposes,
        including scraping content or harvesting contact details for outreach
      </li>
      <li>
        Misrepresent yourself, or imply an association with ArkSystems that does not exist
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="links">7. Links to other sites</h2>

    <p>
      This site links to third-party services, including our booking provider. Following a
      link takes you to a service we do not control and that has its own terms and privacy
      practices. We are not responsible for those services or their content.
    </p>

    <h2 id="availability">8. Availability</h2>

    <p>
      We aim to keep the site available and accurate, but we do not promise that it will be
      uninterrupted, error-free, or current at every moment. We may change, suspend or
      withdraw any part of it without notice.
    </p>

    <h2 id="liability">9. Limitation of liability</h2>

    <p>
      To the fullest extent permitted by law, ArkSystems is not liable for any loss or damage
      arising from your use of this website, or from reliance on anything published on it,
      including lost profits, lost business, lost data or indirect or consequential loss.
    </p>

    <p>
      Nothing in these terms limits liability that cannot be limited by law, including
      liability for fraud, or rights you may have under applicable consumer protection
      legislation.
    </p>

    <h2 id="conflict">10. If these terms conflict with an agreement between us</h2>

    <p>
      If you are a client and we have a signed engagement agreement, statement of work or
      equivalent, that document governs the work and takes precedence over these terms
      wherever they differ. These terms cover your use of the website only.
    </p>

    <h2 id="privacy">11. Privacy</h2>

    <p>
      How we handle personal information is set out in our <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>,
      which forms part of these terms.
    </p>

    <h2 id="governing-law">12. Governing law</h2>

    <p>
      These terms are governed by the laws of the Province of British Columbia and the federal
      laws of Canada that apply there. Any dispute is subject to the exclusive jurisdiction of
      the courts of British Columbia.
    </p>

    <h2 id="changes">13. Changes to these terms</h2>

    <p>
      We may update these terms. The effective date at the top shows when they last changed,
      and the version in force is the one published when you use the site.
    </p>

    <h2 id="contact">14. Contact</h2>

    <div class="doc-contact">
      <p>ArkSystems, operated by {LEGAL_ENTITY}</p>
      {/* Plain text, not a mailto: link — see the note on /privacy section 11. */}
      <p>{LEGAL_EMAIL}</p>
    </div>
  </LegalDocument>
</BaseLayout>
